From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:28:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: mt2701: adapt the AFE to voice streams

The 834-v6 and 854-v6 boards move 8 kHz narrowband PCM through the
MT2701 AFE. Two parts of the driver block that traffic.

period_bytes_min was 1024 and periods_min was 4, which suits music
playback. A 20 ms narrowband frame holds 320 bytes at 16-bit mono, so
the floor forced a period at least three times longer than one voice
frame. Drop the floor to 320 bytes, allow a two period ring, and scale
period_bytes_max and buffer_bytes_max by the same factor.

mt2701_afe_i2s_prepare() returned -EBUSY when the path was occupied.
snd_pcm_prepare() can run again on a prepared stream, for example
after an xrun. Only mt2701_afe_i2s_shutdown() clears occupied, so the
second prepare failed and the stream never recovered. Report success
and leave the running path alone.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt2701/mt2701-afe-pcm.c |   16 +++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt2701/mt2701-afe-pcm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt2701/mt2701-afe-pcm.c
@@ -24,11 +24,11 @@ static const struct snd_pcm_hardware mt2
 		| SNDRV_PCM_INFO_RESUME | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_MMAP_VALID,
 	.formats = SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE
 		   | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE,
-	.period_bytes_min = 1024,
-	.period_bytes_max = 1024 * 256,
-	.periods_min = 4,
+	.period_bytes_min = 320,
+	.period_bytes_max = 320 * 256,
+	.periods_min = 2,
 	.periods_max = 1024,
-	.buffer_bytes_max = 1024 * 1024,
+	.buffer_bytes_max = 320 * 1024,
 	.fifo_size = 0,
 };
 
@@ -240,8 +240,14 @@ static int mt2701_afe_i2s_prepare(struct
 
 	i2s_path = &afe_priv->i2s_path[i2s_num];
 
+	/*
+	 * snd_pcm_prepare() can run again on a stream that is already
+	 * prepared, for example when userspace recovers from an xrun.
+	 * occupied is cleared only in mt2701_afe_i2s_shutdown(), so a
+	 * repeat prepare must report success instead of -EBUSY.
+	 */
 	if (i2s_path->occupied[substream->stream])
-		return -EBUSY;
+		return 0;
 
 	ret = mt2701_mclk_configuration(afe, mode ? 1 : i2s_num);
 	if (ret)
